ingredients:
  - "1 cup split moong dal (yellow or green)"
  - "2-3 green chilies, finely chopped"
  - "1-inch piece of ginger, grated"
  - "Salt to taste"
  - "Ghee"
  - "1 onion, finely chopped"
  - "1 tomato, finely chopped"
  - "1 small carrot"
  - "Fresh coriander leaves, finely chopped"
instructions:
  - "Soak moong dal in water for 4-6 hours. Drain and rinse."
  - "Blend the soaked dal along with green chilies, ginger, and salt to make a smooth batter."
  - "Mix in chopped onions, tomatoes, carrots, and coriander leaves."
  - "Heat a non-stick pan and pour a ladleful of batter. Spread it in a circular motion to make a thin pancake."
  - "Cook on both sides until golden brown with ghee."
  - "Serve hot with chutney or yogurt."
